name       CODE:2BBC6 BALL_END      ; GAME_PHASE 5 (in the port 2026-09-30, docs/HANDOFF.md, "GAME_PHASE 5 in the port")
name       CODE:2AA90 GAME_OVER     ; GAME_PHASE 3 (in the port 2026-09-30, docs/HANDOFF.md, "GAME_PHASE 3 and 8 in the port"): header slot 36's music record, the player's score; each player's score (its record's word +0 and dword +4) against TABLE_HISCORES' five entries (their word +4, dword +6), at or above one HISCORE_ENTER; the initials of CODE:2B09D into the entry reached, which is state+0D2Eh (MULTIBALL_ON and the next two bytes) when none was passed; then state+0E34h FFh (the players' scores in ATTRACT), GAME_PHASE 1
name       CODE:2ABA4 HISCORE_ENTER ; the entries below moved down one, the score into the entry, header slot 37's music record once a game over (CODE:2ADF0), "PLAYER n GOT A HIGHSCORE", three letters typed (KEY_CHARS by LAST_KEY; Backspace takes one back, Enter ends with those typed) into CODE:2B09D, their count CODE:2AFE0
name       CODE:2AFF5 OVER_WAIT     ; [CODE:0020]'s low word x FRAME_RATE frames of OVER_FRAMES
name       CODE:2B012 OVER_FRAMES   ; [CODE:0020]'s low word frames (counted in CODE:2B03E) of FRAME_STEP, PLAY_SCROLL, CODE:156C3 (a RET), FLIPPERS_STEP
name       CODE:2BB3E EXTRA_BALL    ; GAME_PHASE 8: state+0D2Fh FFh (the skill shot armed), header slot 34's music record; frames as BALL_WAIT's with FLASH_STEP, LIT_LIST_STEP and "EXTRA BALL" (CODE:2BBB2) until state+0D3Ch is 0, then GAME_PHASE 4; no ball save (BALL_END set it 0; run 2026-09-30, table 1: the extra ball lost 1.7 s after its launch went to GAME_PHASE 5 at once)
comment    CODE:2A557 after a game over (state+0E34h set by GAME_OVER): "GAME OVER" (CODE:2A92C) while state+0E34h is negative, "PLAYER n" (state+0D72h) and its score while positive, 100 frames each (state+0E36h), the sign flipped at each change; after the players (state+0E2Ah) again from the first, twice (CODE:2A92A; the count CODE:2A928), then state+0E34h 0 (CODE:2A67E); the display stream is not run meanwhile (runs 2026-09-30, table 1, one and two players)
comment    CODE:134D4 the slope map read one line past its end when the ball is below the table's last line: the byte comes from pMAX's header of the next heap block (run 2026-09-30, table 1, the extra ball lost: the map's block at linear 2FFCB0h, C50h bytes, the byte read at 30090Ch, the header's +0Ch, the name's selector 04h, so slope vector 4; the port writes pMAX's headers since, docs/HANDOFF.md, "pMAX's heap headers")
name       CODE:29BE1 LIGHTS_BALL_RESET ; at the next ball: LIGHTS_RESET but in a group with bit 2 of its byte +4 set, where a light keeps its picture, its state+16B2h byte and its +5
name       CODE:29CE3 RECORDS_BALL_RESET ; at the next ball: header slot 15's records as RECORDS_RESET, the player's bit ([CODE:0038] AND 7) cleared in +2 unless bit 5 of +0, in +1 unless bit 0; lit (+1 FFh) with bit 1; those lit for the player back on the lit list; then STREAMS_RESET
name       CODE:2A113 COUNTERS_BALL_RESET ; at the next ball: header slot 16's counters' +38h, +3Ch, +26h 0; without bit 0 of +0 as COUNTERS_RESET for the player only (+30h, +34h from +28h, +2Ch unless bit 3, the player's words +6 and +16h, the thresholds' bytes +2); with it the 12-digit number ending at +38h added to the one ending at +40h (the player's word +6) times; then slot 17's lists as COUNTERS_RESET
name       CODE:2C037 FRAMES_WAIT   ; host vector +0Ch: [CODE:0020] fiftieths of a second of frames (x FRAME_RATE / 50), the scroll, flippers, flashes and lights stepped; after the first half second a key (LAST_KEY) ends it; [CODE:0010] kept
name       CODE:4FF9 CHOOSER
name       CODE:B9B9 DRV_FRAME
