name       CODE:00A3 OPT_SVGA_MODE ; OPTIONS+6, not a line of the options screen: the mode MODE_SVGA640/800 set; up to 13h a VESA mode 100h+it (INT 10h AX=4F02h), above it a BIOS mode (AX=00xxh); found by SVGA_FIND, 0 again when the resolution is changed on the options screen (CODE:32D5A). Runs 2026-09-29 (doskit's VESA): 1 for SVGA 640x480, then mode 101h
code       CODE:0753 SVGA_CHECK    ; at the start (called at CODE:0320), when OPT_RESOLUTION is 1 or 2 (SVGA): OPT_SVGA_MODE set by INT 10h AH=0 and checked (CODE:0649); if that fails or it is 0, SVGA_FIND with CL 3 (640x480) or 5 (800x600); nothing found: OPT_RESOLUTION 0 (VGA 360x350); the options written back to the configuration file (INT 94h AH=6). In the port 2026-10-01 as a VESA card answers (docs/HANDOFF.md, "The SVGA modes in the port")
code       CODE:05FF SVGA_FIND     ; CL 3 or 5: an S3 BIOS ("S3" in the first 100h bytes at C0000h, CODE:0581) gives 49h or 4Bh; else VESA (CODE:05BE: AX=4F00h answers 4Fh and the block starts "VESA") gives CL-2, i.e. 1 or 3; else the BIOS modes 14h..7Fh are set one by one (CODE:0621) and the first that passes CODE:0649 is taken: chain-4 on, the DAC reads back what was written (as read, not run), for CL 3 the misc register's bits 6, 7 and CR 1 4Fh or 9Fh (640 wide at 8 or 4 pixels a character clock); CL 5 not followed
comment    CODE:97A4 SVGA at 640x480 (MODE_SVGA800 alike: 800x600, 64h instead of 50h to CODE:95B5, the split at 568, FRAME_RATE 3Ch too): OPT_SVGA_MODE set, then as VGA 360 does it: planar (CODE:957E: chain-4 off, byte mode), the line 336 pixels wide (CODE:95A1: CR 1 29h, or 53h where the card's CR 1 was above 96h, i.e. 4 pixels a character clock), the horizontal retrace moved by half the width taken off, presumably to centre it (CODE:95B5, BL the mode's width in character clocks, 50h), CR 13h 2Ah (84 bytes a line, as in VGA 360), the split (line compare) at 448: the table above, the 32-line display below. So SVGA shows more lines of the table, not a wider one. Runs 2026-09-29 (doskit's VESA, OPT_RESOLUTION poked): 336x480 and 336x600 pictures, FRAME_RATE measured 3Bh at 60 Hz and 3Ch at 60.3 Hz
; Esc on a table (2026-09-29; run on table 1, see docs/HANDOFF.md, "Esc")
name       CODE:CBCC GAME_PHASE    ; state+8Eh: the number by which CODE:BAD6's routines are called each round (CODE:B993). Run 2026-09-29 (table 1, a game of three balls, -watch): 1 attract mode (CODE:2A4F8); F1: 2 game start (2A976), at once 6 the ball waits for its launch (2B1DC, "PLAYER 1 BALL n"); Enter: 4 play (2B76E); 7 a lost ball served again while the ball save runs (2BAD5, "DON'T MOVE"; from CODE:2B946), back to 4 after about 1.3 s; 5 the ball lost (2BBC6, the bonus, "NO BONUS"), then 6, or 8 for an extra ball (2BB3E, "EXTRA BALL"; seen with the player's byte +10h poked: set by 2BC0B, 4 again by 2BBA8 at the Enter that launches the ball), or after the last ball 3 game over (2AA90, "GAME OVER"), then 1. Esc during play 3 (CODE:2BAB5), Esc in phase 6 1 (CODE:2B345). 9 the tilt (2B716, set by CODE:2B918 while state+2A75h is set; run: three nudges, "TILT" shown, the ball lost 0.85 s later without a flipper press, 5 and 6 in the same frame, no bonus); 0 (CODE:BAFE) written by no instruction (all 18 writes are the constants 1..9; the image's 0 is replaced by 1 at CODE:B928 before the loop); poked in a run it hangs the game (see CODE:BAFE)
name       CODE:CBCB QUIT_TABLE    ; state+8Dh: FFh leaves the table for the chooser (run: written by CODE:2BABB at t=140.01, Esc during play; the chooser's screens followed)
comment    CODE:2A8AB Esc in the attract mode: the text "REALLY QUIT TABLE?" (CODE:2A93E) while the frame step goes on, until KEY_DOWN+15h (scan code 15h, Y on a QWERTY keyboard: yes, QUIT_TABLE FFh) or another key (LAST_KEY; on with the attract mode) (run: Esc at t=124 showed the text, Space at 127 went on; 2026-09-30, table 1: Esc at 150, Y at 152 ended the main loop at CODE:BA7C; N at 152 went on, the attract record queued again). The loop calls FLIPPERS_STEP, so a key read there (Space, Alt: a nudge) acts already while the question is up
comment    CODE:2B63B the same question for Esc at CODE:2B56D (the routine at CODE:2B543, its callers not followed; presumably while the ball waits for its launch, not run): Y QUIT_TABLE FFh, another key back to CODE:2B543
name       CODE:2BAD3 LOST_BALL_RUNOUT ; FFh while CODE:2B9F6 runs the streams out after a lost ball; read only by MUSIC_REQUEST (run 2026-09-29, -rwatch)
comment    CODE:2B716 GAME_PHASE 9, the tilt: a frame of play (FRAME_STEP, CODE:2B49A, 1023E, the zones and events CODE:2B4B9) with no flipper keys read (not traced: that the flippers are dead is presumed from play's CODE:2B76E having the key reads this lacks), "TILT" on the display (CODE:27783); a lost ball to CODE:2B9F6. BONUS_ADD pays nothing while state+2A75h is set; CODE:122C1 and 12304 skip their work then (not followed). State+2A75h and +2A78h cleared at the next ball (CODE:2BBC6...). Run 2026-09-29, table 1: 145.21 to 146.06. In the port 2026-10-01 (docs/HANDOFF.md, "GAME_PHASE 9 in the port"): state+2A7Fh 0 each frame, which FLIPPERS_MOVE asks before a flipper goes up
comment    CODE:2B9F6 a lost ball without the ball save (from play at CODE:2B946 when the ball save's count state+0D3Eh is 0, and from GAME_PHASE 9, CODE:2B716; both after CODE:2C0C7 comes back negative): state+0D51h and LOST_BALL_RUNOUT FFh, then frames stepped here until the two event streams (state+2A28h/2A2Ah, 2A1Ch/2A1Eh) and the mode stream (state+0D5Eh) are empty; then both 0 and GAME_PHASE 5. Runs 2026-09-29, table 1, no flipper: with no stream running FFh for 14 ms (t=155.951 to 155.965); with START MODE forced as in HANDOFF's "A mode's track in a run", the ball lost at t=148.494 during the mode, the mode's closing record (the one its timer brings at t=197.3 when no ball is lost) through MUSIC_REQUEST's bit-1 branch at t=148.621; that the mode stream gets there through state+0D51h (CODE:2CD3C) is presumed, not traced
comment    CODE:2BAB5 Esc during play (CODE:2B76E): QUIT_TABLE FFh and GAME_PHASE 3 at once, no question (run: Esc at t=140 in a game, the screen dark at 141, the chooser's table menu after Space at 144; Esc there at 150: "Thank you for playing Pinball Illusions CD." and exit code 32)
comment    CODE:9D3C the track's time up, a return set: CD volume 0, the driver's command 8 with the order index and slot of CODE:9CE6/9CE8 (run 2026-09-29, table 2: at t=151.03, after track 19 of the music chooser)
comment    CODE:9E13 a track in MUSIC_NEXT: the record's order index and module slot kept in CODE:9CE6/9CE8 (the module music to return to), the module request cleared, the track played, CD volume C0h; when its time is up (CODE:9CEA) the driver's command 8 with them, the CD volume 0 (9CE6 0: the track again)
comment    CODE:9E83 the module request (state+2A84h): positive (1, 2, 3, 6, 7, 8 in the four modules' slot-34 records; only the sign is read, by this CMP) the driver's command 0Ah (temporary module playback, docs/audio-driver.md: a jingle in place of the module's music, which then goes on from where it stopped; run 2026-09-29, table 1, record 11F15h's words poked here: 1.78 s, the 89 ticks of music2.mod's pattern 14 at 50 Hz) with BX the order index, CX the module slot, the CD volume 0 first when bit 2 of CODE:CB97 is set (byte +0Ah 4 in 12/20/18/0 of the jingle records of tables 1..4; run 2026-09-29, table 1 with track 4 playing: CD volume 0 at t=151.434, C0h again at the jingle's end, t=154.162, CODE:9DC7); negative: CD volume 0, the track's countdown CODE:9DBD stopped (-1), command 8 (the module from that order index); 0: nothing
comment    CODE:9B76 module slots 0 and 1 loaded above from CODE:98D5 and 98E9 (data\s00n\music.mod and music2.mod, the digit at CODE:98DD/98F1; slot 1 not when CODE:A311 is 4); command 8, order index 1 of slot 0: the module music at a table's start
comment    CODE:2B345 the module request without a record: order index 1, slot 0, word FFFEh (state+8Eh = 1)
comment    CODE:2ABA4 the score (CODE:0020/0024) against the list of 10-byte entries at state+C0CFCh: the first time an entry is passed, header slot 37's record (tracks 8, 18, 34, 48 for tables 1..4); presumably the high-score music (reached 2026-09-30 with a poked score, NOSOUND: the track not looked at)
comment    CODE:2AA90 header slot 36's record (track 0, byte +0Ah 2 in all four tables; run, table 1: once, at t=193.8, what happened then not looked at)
comment    CODE:2B1DC header slot 34's record, record 0 (track 0; run, table 1: at t=130.0, the F1 start, 135.8 and 147.2)
comment    CODE:2B8ED header slot 38's record while state+2A75h is set (track 0 in all four tables); runs every frame in a game
comment    CODE:3007A by the type of the record at [CODE:0000] (its first byte AND 7): 4, an audio record, to MUSIC_REQUEST; 2 to CODE:9F2C (run, table 1: record 42, track 0, came from none of the other callers logged; this way, presumably)
; the tracks of the table's modes (2026-09-29, from the four modules' data
; and the handlers below; no such play seen in a run yet)
comment    CODE:2D9DE the word +2Ch of the slot-15 record at [CODE:0008] picks one of the handlers at CODE:2DA0A (0: none)
name       CODE:2DCA1 TAKE_COUNT_STREAM
comment    CODE:2DCA1 handler 6 of CODE:2DA0A: the record's dword +34h is a slot-16 counter; the current player's word +6 of it counted up, at the limit (word +4) its stream +48h to EVENT_QUEUE; then CODE:2DD8A
comment    CODE:2DD8A the counter's threshold actions (12 bytes from +50h): the one reached has its dword +4, an event stream, go to EVENT_QUEUE (at CODE:2DD75)
comment    CODE:2E5A2 handler 11h of CODE:2DA0A: the record's dword +34h is an event stream, to EVENT_QUEUE
name       CODE:2FE8E EVENT_QUEUE  ; [CODE:0000] into the ring of 64 dwords at [state+2A1Eh], the index state+2A1Ah
; how a mode starts (2026-09-29; run on table 1 with two -poke, see
; docs/HANDOFF.md, "A mode's track in a run")
comment    CODE:2C1DA each ball of the list at state+C1046h (state+C0D32h of them): its centre (words +12h, +14h, plus 8 each) against the zones at its dword +64h (14 bytes: x0, y0, x1, y1, a type, an object; -1 ends them; header slots 5 and 11 in table 1); inside one, the type through CODE:2C3DD. The ball's byte +0Ah marks the object while it is inside (type 4 in the object's byte +1, types 0 and 1 in byte +0), so a zone acts on entry, presumably (run: table 1's zone 3447h widened, its object's stream ran 0.56 s later)
name       CODE:2E08C TAKE_COUNT
comment    CODE:2E08C handler 15h of CODE:2DA0A: as handler 6 (CODE:2DCA1) without its end: the counter at +34h counted up for the current player, its word +16h too, then CODE:2DD8A (run, table 1: record 41E6h, counter 421Eh, at the ball's launch and in bursts; +16h back to 1 after 9 at CODE:2DF20)
name       CODE:2E5B7 TAKE_LEVEL_STREAM
comment    CODE:2E5B7 handler 16h of CODE:2DA0A: the counter at +34h's threshold action equal to the current player's word +16h: its stream (+4) to EVENT_QUEUE (table 1: record 4362h, lit by zone 352Fh's stream, taken by zone 3447h's; run with it forced: threshold 1, opcode 9, the mode stream's opcode 13h plays track 4)
comment    CODE:4FE8 plays track 33h (51) at the chooser's loading of infodata.mgl; not reached in runs up to t=126 (the chooser at t=7 plays no track)
; the other slot-15 handlers (2026-09-29, read from the code and the four
; modules' records; no run made for the handlers). "The player" is the
; record at state+0D76h (CODE:D8B8, player 1, in runs): its +8 a 12-digit
; packed-BCD number (high word +0, low dword +4) shown by display opcode
; 8, the score; its +10h another (high word +8, low dword +0Ch), the
; bonus (CODE:2BD95); byte +10h, byte +11h, word +12h, byte +14h below.
; The names checked in runs 2026-09-29 (table 1, docs/HANDOFF.md, "The
; player record in a run"): the takes raise +8 only; the bonus 12,345
; with word +12h 3 poked at a lost ball adds 37,035 to +8, the screen
; shows "BONUS 12,345", then "EXTRA BALL" for byte +10h 1
comment    CODE:2FBBF a take's points: [CODE:000C] points past a 12-digit packed-BCD number (high word at -8, low dword at -4), added to the player's +10h; the number 8 bytes before it added to the player's +8 (for a slot-15 record's +2Ch: +24h/+28h to +10h, +1Ch/+20h to +8; table 1 has records with both, e.g. 1000000 and 500000)
comment    CODE:2FD11 the 12-digit number [CODE:000C] points past added to the player's +8; CODE:2FDD3 the same to the player's +10h
comment    CODE:2BD95 at a lost ball (from CODE:2BBC6): the player's +10h number added to state+2AC8h/2ACCh once, or word +12h times when that is above 1, and that sum later to the player's +8 (after the call through state+2926h): the bonus times its multiplier (run: 12,345 x 3 in the score 2.0 to 2.2 s after the loss, between two dumps)
comment    CODE:2A4B1 the player's +10h number cleared unless byte +11h is set, word +12h cleared unless byte +14h is set; both bytes cleared: the bonus and its multiplier held for one ball (run: with both bytes FFh the bonus and the 3 stayed, the bytes 0)
comment    CODE:2BBC6 the player's byte +10h: not 0, one less and state+8Eh = 8 (after the text "EXTRA BALL" at CODE:2BBB2): extra balls (run: 1 poked, "EXTRA BALL" shown, GAME_PHASE 8 until the launch, the byte 0)
name       CODE:2E2E1 TAKE_EXTRA_BALL
comment    CODE:2E2E1 handler 1 of CODE:2DA0A: the first light state of header slot 25 (state+290Ah) gets byte +5 FFh, the player's byte +10h one more: an extra ball (the records' +34h not read)
name       CODE:2E31C TAKE_HOLD_BONUS
comment    CODE:2E31C handler 2 of CODE:2DA0A: byte +0 of [+34h] set to FFh when that is not 0 (table 2's one such record, 7402h, has 2 there, the next record's first word, so CODE:0002 is written, a scratch dword rewritten at once), the player's bit (CODE:003C, presumably) into byte +0 of the light state at +8, the player's byte +11h FFh (bonus held, CODE:2A4B1)
comment    CODE:2E6AB handler 3 of CODE:2DA0A: the player's +10h number added to its +8 (in no record of the four tables)
name       CODE:2E43A TAKE_MULTIPLIER
comment    CODE:2E43A handler 5 of CODE:2DA0A: the player's word +12h = the record's word +34h (2, 4, 6, 8, 0Ah in five records of tables 1, 2 and 4; 2..5 in four of table 3): the bonus multiplier, presumably
name       CODE:2E6CC TAKE_SCORE
comment    CODE:2E6CC handler 7 of CODE:2DA0A: the slot-16 counter at +34h: its value (high word +38h, low dword +3Ch) added to the player's +8
name       CODE:2E37F TAKE_HOLD_MULT
comment    CODE:2E37F handler 8 of CODE:2DA0A: the player's byte +14h FFh (multiplier held, CODE:2A4B1; in table 1 only)
comment    CODE:2E2C0 handler 9 of CODE:2DA0A: the player's +8 added to itself (in no record)
name       CODE:2E6EA TAKE_SCORE_TIMES
comment    CODE:2E6EA handler 0Ah of CODE:2DA0A: the counter at +34h's value (as handler 7) added to the player's +8 as many times as the record's word +38h, or the current player's count (word +6) when that is less, and then that count set to 0; the count is not lowered otherwise (table 1's record 7C64h, the word 19h)
name       CODE:2E13D TAKE_RAISE
comment    CODE:2E13D handler 0Bh of CODE:2DA0A: the counter at +34h's value (+38h/+3Ch) raised by its step (high word +30h, low dword +34h; from +28h/+2Ch at CODE:2DF5C), then set to +40h/+44h when both dwords are at or above those and +40h is not negative: a cap, presumably
comment    CODE:2E29F handler 0Dh of CODE:2DA0A: the player's +10h added to itself (in no record)
name       CODE:2E778 TAKE_SCORE_STEP
comment    CODE:2E778 handler 0Eh of CODE:2DA0A: the counter at +34h's step (+30h/+34h) added to the player's +8
name       CODE:2E45C TAKE_STEP_ADD
comment    CODE:2E45C handler 0Fh of CODE:2DA0A: the counter at +34h's step raised by the record's number at +38h/+3Ch (e.g. 5000000 in table 2's record 5F5Ah)
comment    CODE:2DC91 handler 10h of CODE:2DA0A: handlers 0Bh, 6 and 7 in turn
comment    CODE:2DC86 handler 12h of CODE:2DA0A: handlers 0Bh and 6 in turn
name       CODE:2E796 TAKE_BCD_SCORE
comment    CODE:2E796 handler 13h of CODE:2DA0A: [+34h] is a slot-26 BCD counter (so in all four tables): its current value (+2, +6) copied to its +22h, +26h and added to the player's +8
name       CODE:2E7C8 TAKE_TIMER
comment    CODE:2E7C8 handler 14h of CODE:2DA0A: the counter at +34h's word +26h = the record's word +38h times FRAME_RATE (state+50h): the time until COUNTER_TIMERS puts the counter's step back and its value to 0 (records 579Ch, 57D6h of table 1, 5 and 10 s, counter 574Ah; 490Ch of table 3, 12 s, counter 48BAh)
name       CODE:2E21D TAKE_MODE_TIME
comment    CODE:2E21D handler 17h of CODE:2DA0A: while the mode stream waits with a timer (state+0D50h, 0D62h not negative) the timer set to the smaller of the record's words +34h and +36h times FRAME_RATE (state+50h); the timer plus +34h is computed (CODE:0024) and not used (table 3's record 75C4h: 5 and 1Eh, so 5 s)
name       CODE:2E7FC TAKE_UNCOUNT
comment    CODE:2E7FC handler 18h of CODE:2DA0A: the counter at +34h's words +6 and +16h of the current player one less, unless +6 is 0
comment    CODE:2E396 handler 19h of CODE:2DA0A: as handler 0Fh with DAS: the step lowered by the record's number (in no record)
name       CODE:2E51D TAKE_RANDOM
comment    CODE:2E51D handler 1Ah of CODE:2DA0A: a number 0..FFh from the low byte of CODE:BAD4 (the counter display opcode 1Ah blinks by, CODE:2F7DE); [+34h] is a list of 8-byte entries (flags word, limit word, event stream): the first whose limit is above the number has its stream queued, unless its flag bit 0 is set and bit 1 set already (set here), then the number plus 5Dh again: a random award, each with bit 0 once (tables 2 and 4, 8 entries each, the last limit 100h); the number is so the frame count's low byte (DRV_TICK). Table 4's record 5662h: 8 entries of 32 each, all with bit 0 (light 5728h, takes 4F3Ah, 5790h, 575Ch, 57C4h, three empty); 5662h is lit only by threshold 15 of counter 55F6h, whose word +16h is per player and reset only at the game start (CODE:29FFA; flag bit 0 keeps it at CODE:2A113), so at most one award per player and game, eight at most: the loop at CODE:2E56D, endless once all eight are given, is not reached (by the code, not run). Bit 1 is cleared only at the game start (CODE:2A0C2) and is shared by the players
name       CODE:2E506 TAKE_STEP_ADD2
comment    CODE:2E506 handler 1Bh of CODE:2DA0A: as handler 0Fh with the number past [+38h]+8 (in table 3 a slot-26 counter +2: its current value)

