words      CODE:26957 4 CODE       ; called at CODE:26946 by the byte at CODE:A311 less one (compared with 4 elsewhere; values 1..4 presumed)
words      CODE:26967 4 CODE       ; called at CODE:269AC, the same way
words      CODE:30D78 2 CODE       ; jumped to at CODE:30D76 by the word at [ESI+0Eh]; two pointers, zeros after them (the index range not checked)
; compiled switches: 16-bit offsets from the table (MOV reg,T[reg*2];
; LEA reg,[reg+T]; JMP/CALL reg); the index mostly the previous entry,
; kept in a dword at CODE:0020..0028. Counts from the bound check where there is one, else
; up to the smallest offset (the code right after the table)
rwords     CODE:1183F 20           ; CODE:117EB; index checked against 1Fh at CODE:117D9
rwords     CODE:11AE9 8            ; CODE:11A92, CODE:11AD0; index a byte ([[CODE:0000]+1]); eight, as 78h data words follow (CODE:11AF9, read at CODE:11A61 with an index below 78h) up to the first target
code       CODE:14DE2              ; MOV EBX,14DE2h; CALL EBX at CODE:298CA
rwords     CODE:13784 8            ; CODE:13725
rwords     CODE:2C3DD 5            ; CODE:2C2DF, by a zone's type (word +8, see CODE:2C1DA); the smallest offset is 32h, what lies from CODE:2C3E7 on is not checked
rwords     CODE:2C8BC 3            ; CODE:2C887
rwords     CODE:2F91C 2            ; CODE:2F903; index the complement of the word at CODE:0020 (the record's word +2: FFFFh 0, FFFEh 1); the two arms are the same code
rwords     CODE:300B9 8            ; CODE:300A0; index the low three bits of a byte (CODE:30099)
rwords     CODE:308C7 2            ; CODE:308AD
name       CODE:A448 TABLE_END     ; TABLE after the game: IRQ 1's vector back (CODE:A01E), TABLE_FADE_OUT, TABLE_SOUND_END, HISCORES_PUT, CODE:28D17 (LIGHTS_SEL, DROPS_SEL, MASKS_SEL but on table 2 freed), DM_FREE, VM_DATA_FREE (not on table 3), CODE:A4E1, the BLOCKS list (CODE:A55E) and the ALLOCS list (CODE:A52E, INT 92h AH=2) freed last first, then CODE:A499; in C in port/src/table.c, compared 2026-10-01 (docs/HANDOFF.md, "The table's end and the chooser again")
name       CODE:A6B4 TABLE_FADE_OUT ; 32 pictures from the stage's palette toward TBL_PALETTE, the driver's command 6 after each with BX FFh less 8 a picture
name       CODE:9FB1 TABLE_SOUND_END ; CD_STOP between two SND_PAUSEs (command 2, a toggle), the driver's commands 3, 5 (slot 0; slot 1 but on table 4) and 0Bh, the code alias at CODE:98A4 freed (INT 93h AH=0Dh)
name       CODE:7182 DRIVER_RELOAD ; after a table (ENTRY's loop): the driver of the configuration header loaded and started again, CHOOSER_MOD_NAME into slot 0, command 0Ch with 0; in C in port/src/sound.c
code       CODE:A4A9               ; far jump at CODE:A4A3 through CODE:A2C1, with the selector saved from CS at CODE:A36A; then TBL_DRIVER_SEL, TABLE_DS and CS's alias freed with INT 93h AH=0Dh: the driver's block stays allocated (the run's heap at CODE:7182)
code       CODE:4DB7               ; pushed at CODE:4D90 as the return address of the routine that ends in XCHG [ESP],EBX (CODE:4DB3); RET
words      CODE:29912 4 CODE       ; called in turn at CODE:298A7 through the pointer at CODE:2982E, which holds 29912h in the file; CODE:29873 (not reached yet) sets it to 29922h, a like table of four after this one
words      CODE:7AC0 0C0 CODE stride=8 ; records of 8 bytes from CODE:7ABC to 80BCh, a dword ascending (presumably a time) and a handler: CODE:704E calls [ESI+4] while [CODE:8124] reaches the first dword ([CODE:8128] set to 7ABCh at CODE:789A)
; two interpreters of word streams (the stream's word an index, 0 ends it):
; records of 4 bytes, a 16-bit offset from the table's second record and a
; number added to the stream's position; no bound check, the counts are up
; to the code after the table (its first offset)
rwords     CODE:2D18F 20 stride=4 from=2D193 ; LEA at CODE:2CF36 and CODE:2D148, call through CODE:2CF57 and CODE:2D169; record 0 leads to a RET
rwords     CODE:2F625 1A stride=4 from=2F625 ; LEA at CODE:2F4A4 and CODE:2F5A2, call through CODE:2F4C5 and CODE:2F5C4; record 0 at CODE:2F621 is 0,0 (index 0 not called)
; the event language (2026-09-29, read from the handlers; the operand kinds
; checked on the four modules with tools/event_streams.py: every stream it
; finds parses to its end with relocated pointers, none in both languages).
; A position is a byte offset from the stream's first command.
comment    CODE:2D080 the event queue's runner: the stream at state+2A22h, else the next of the ring at [state+2A1Eh] (index state+2A1Ch, filled by EVENT_QUEUE); one command a call, by the table at CODE:2D18F (record n at +4n: the handler's offset from CODE:2D193 and the command's size, added to the stream's position word +2 before the call); commands from +4, opcode 0 ends the stream
comment    CODE:2CD3C the mode stream (state+0D5Eh, from event opcode 9), one command a call from CODE:2CEF1; while opcode 1Ch waits (state+0D50h) its timer state+0D62h counts down (whole seconds to state+2A6Eh, 2A6Fh) and the stream goes on at its next command once the record at state+0D66h is no longer lit for the player, or at the position state+0D6Ah when the time is up (CODE:2CE98); while it waits and opcode 1Bh's multiball (state+0D2Eh) is down to one ball (state+0D51h), at the position state+0D6Ch (opcode 1Eh; 0: state+0D6Ah)
comment    CODE:2D36E event opcode 1 (a slot-15 record): lit for the current player (its bit, CODE:0038, in byte +1) unless lit already or blocked (byte +2); newly lit: its lamp (the light state at +4) on unless a mode runs and flag bit 4 (byte +0) is set, its +0Ch through CODE:3007A, its display stream +14h through CODE:2FEDB; then no timer (+2Eh = -1) and the record on the list at state+2A32h (once: bit 2 of byte +0)
comment    CODE:2D491 event opcode 2 (a slot-15 record, a word): as opcode 1, lit for a time: nothing when blocked, the lamp, +0Ch and +14h each time; +2Eh = the word times FRAME_RATE (state+50h), counted down on the list by LIT_LIST_STEP
name       CODE:2D67E OP_BLOCK
comment    CODE:2D67E event opcode 3 (a slot-15 record): blocked for the current player (byte +2): its lamp off (CODE:2E82F), unlit when its timer runs and flag bit 1 is clear, the timer stopped (+2Eh = -1)
comment    CODE:2D23E event opcode 4 (an object, a word): when the object's word +0 is 1, its byte +0Bh cleared and the word (0, 1 or FFFFh in the modules) to CODE:28E5D, into the table at CODE:288DC by the object's number at +44h (1..0Ah in the modules); DROPS_DRAW draws it on a change: the object is a drop target, the word its state (0 up, else down)
comment    CODE:2D907 event opcode 5 (a slot-15 record): taken (CODE:2D916) when lit for the current player and not blocked: unlit, its points (CODE:2FBBF: packed BCD, the word +24h and dword +28h, e.g. 05000000h, to the player's +10h, the bonus presumably; +1Ch/+20h to its +8), lit again when flag bit 1 or 3 is set, else its lamp off; its display stream +18h through CODE:2FEDB, the player's bit in byte +5 of the light state at +8, its +10h through CODE:3007A, then its handler by the word +2Ch (CODE:2D9DE)
comment    CODE:2D827 event opcode 6 (a slot-16 counter): its dwords +28h, +2Ch to +30h, +34h
comment    CODE:2D8A6 event opcode 7 (a slot-16 counter, two dwords): the dwords to the counter's +30h, +34h
name       CODE:2D785 OP_HOLE
comment    CODE:2D785 event opcode 8 (a hole: the object of a type-4 zone): bit 1 cleared, +34h 0, pushed on the stack at state+2A64h (down from FA48h); CODE:30BD6 takes them one at a time, CODE:30CFB puts the ball the hole holds (byte +1) out at the hole's +6, +8 with the speed +0Ah, +0Ch on the level +0Eh: an eject
name       CODE:2DA7B OP_MODE_START
comment    CODE:2DA7B event opcode 9 (an event stream): unless state+0D4Fh is set, the stream becomes the running mode stream (state+0D5Eh, state+0D4Fh FFh, the wait and loop state cleared) and the records on the list at state+2A32h with flag bit 4 get their lamps off for the player; in the modules the stream with the mode's opcode 13h (its CD track) is started only this way
comment    CODE:2D5F4 event opcode 0Ah (a position): the stream's position: a jump
name       CODE:2D210 OP_BALL_SAVE
comment    CODE:2D210 event opcode 0Bh (a word): BALL_SAVE = the word times FRAME_RATE (state+50h), counted down a frame at CODE:2B86B; while it runs a lost ball is served again (before CODE:2C1A5, and CODE:2B946) and the lamp at header slot 25's second pointer blinks (CODE:2B883): a ball save of that many seconds (the save seen in runs with the serve's SERVE_SECONDS, this opcode not run)
comment    CODE:2DB8E event opcode 0Ch (a slot-15 record): unblocked for the current player (byte +2)
comment    CODE:2D274 event opcode 0Dh (a slot-16 counter): reset: +30h, +34h from +28h, +2Ch, the current player's words +6 and +16h to the word +2, +38h and +3Ch 0; each threshold (12 bytes from +50h, to a negative one) gets the player's bit in byte +2 cleared and its lamp (+8) off
comment    CODE:2D326 event opcode 0Eh (a slot-15 record): unless flag bit 1 is set, unlit for the current player and its lamp off
comment    CODE:2DB5C event opcode 0Fh (a slot-26 BCD counter): started: its start value (+0Ah, +0Eh) to the current one (+2, +6), byte +0 FFh; moved by CODE:2EACF (docs/bpc-module.md, slot 26)
comment    CODE:2DB7B event opcode 10h (a slot-26 BCD counter): stopped (byte +0 cleared)
comment    CODE:2D6F9 event opcode 11h (a display stream): to CODE:2FEDB, the display queue
comment    CODE:2D843 event opcode 12h (a slot-16 counter, two dwords): the dwords to +38h, +3Ch
comment    CODE:2D5E0 event opcode 13h (an audio record): to MUSIC_REQUEST (run, table 1: record 1, track 0)
comment    CODE:2DBAD event opcode 14h (an object of the module): to state+2A70h, the host vector to [CODE:0010], the object's dword +0 called (PUSH, RET); CODE:2CFC8 calls its +4 later (docs/bpc-module.md, "Deferred event dispatch"; table 2's is the music chooser, "Table 2's music chooser" there)
comment    CODE:2CFC8 when no event stream runs and the queue's next entry is empty (further tests of state+2A2Eh and +2A28h not followed): the module object's +4 (state+2A70h) called with the host vector in [CODE:0010]; its return with ZF clear ends it (state+2A70h and 2A74h cleared, state+2A7Fh FFh), with ZF set it is called again
comment    CODE:2D85F event opcode 15h (a slot-16 counter, a word): the current player's words +6 and +16h = the word
comment    CODE:2D7F9 event opcode 16h (a slot-16 counter): the current player's words +6 and +16h = the counter's word +2
comment    CODE:2D8C2 event opcode 17h (a slot-15 record, a position): unless the record is lit for the current player and not blocked (bytes +1, +2), a jump to the position: past the take that follows, in table 1's stream 4F50h
name       CODE:2D7BE OP_HOLE2
comment    CODE:2D7BE event opcode 18h (a hole, a second hole): as opcode 8, with bit 1 set and the second hole in +34h, whose +6..+0Eh CODE:30CEC takes instead: the ball comes out at the second hole (table 1's modes: held in 4F18h, out at 4DB0h)
comment    CODE:2D358 event opcode 19h: when state+0E44h (RES_CODE, 0..3) is 5, a call of CODE:B927, a RET: no effect (in the modules as often as opcode 1Bh)
name       CODE:2D60A OP_HOLE_SERVE
comment    CODE:2D60A event opcode 1Ah (a hole): its ball (byte +1 less one, an index into state+C107Ah) let go (bit 1 and byte +1 cleared, +34h 0) and put at 11Ch, 1FEh (CODE:29A5A; the plunger lane, presumably); balls on the table (state+0D32h) one less, to be served (state+0D3Ah) one more
name       CODE:2D70E OP_MULTIBALL
comment    CODE:2D70E event opcode 1Bh (a word, at most 0Dh): balls to be served (state+0D3Ah) added until they and those on the table (state+0D32h) are the word; state+0D2Eh FFh, watched by CODE:2CD3C: a multiball
name       CODE:2DBDF OP_MODE_WAIT
comment    CODE:2DBDF event opcode 1Ch (a slot-15 record or 0, a word, a position): the mode stream waits (state+0D50h, see CODE:2CD3C): the record, when lit, to state+0D66h; the word times FRAME_RATE (state+50h) to state+0D62h (0: on at once to the position; negative: no timer); the position to state+0D6Ah
comment    CODE:2D6CC event opcode 1Dh (a position): while the count at state+0D6Eh is not 0, it is counted down and the stream goes to the position: a loop
comment    CODE:2D88D event opcode 1Eh (a position): to state+0D6Ch, where a waiting mode stream goes once the multiball is down to one ball
comment    CODE:2D5C7 event opcode 1Fh (a word): the loop count state+0D6Eh (opcode 1Dh)
; the lit records' timers and the lamps (2026-09-29, read from the code and
; the four modules' header slot 14; no run made for it). A light state
; (docs/bpc-module.md, slot 14) as these routines use it: byte +0 and
; byte +5 a bit a player (on), +1 FFh or 0 (the blink phase; 0: dark),
; +2 bit 1 blinking, bit 2 not drawn, +3 the blink count, +4 its reload
name       CODE:2E8CD LIT_LIST_STEP ; the list of lit slot-15 records, a frame
name       CODE:2CB69 COUNTER_TIMERS ; the slot-16 counters' timers (list at state+28E6h), a frame of play (from CODE:2B4B9): word +26h not 0 counted down; at 0 the step (+30h, +34h) from +28h, +2Ch and the value (+38h, +3Ch) 0, and then RET: the counters after it in the list miss this frame's count (a slip, presumably; no table has two timed counters). Run 2026-09-29, table 1, counter 574Ah poked (+26h 131h, step 5,000,000, value 3,000,000): 0 after 4.35 s (305 frames), the step 1,000,000 and the value 0 again (CODE:2CBA6); 826 calls to t=150. Also 0 in the resets CODE:29FFA and 2A113
comment    CODE:2E8CD once a frame (CODE:2B4B9 in play, and the loop at CODE:2BB5C) along the slot-15 records on the list at state+2A32h (last state+2A36h, next +30h; flag bit 2 while on it), for the current player (state+0D72h, its bit state+0D74h): a record not lit for the player (byte +1), or whose timer +2Eh is 0, is unlit, its lamp off (LAMP_OFF), +2Eh 0, flag bit 2 cleared, and it leaves the list; a timer above 0 is counted down one, and while it is then at most FRAME_RATE (the last game second) the lamp is put off each frame; otherwise, and with no timer (+2Eh negative), the lamp is put on blinking each frame (the player's bit in its byte +0, byte +2 bit 1, +4 = 8) unless the record is blocked for the player (byte +2); neither while a mode runs (state+0D5Eh) and flag bit 4 is set. So opcode 2 with n seconds: the lamp blinks for n-1 game seconds, is dark for the last, and the record is unlit n x FRAME_RATE + 1 frames after (run 2026-09-29, table 1: the skill shot's record 43D2h lit for 5 s at t=138.267, +2Eh 131h (305), 7 less every 0.1 s, the lamp's byte +1 FFh/00h in turn, bytes +0 and +2 cleared from +2Eh 3Ch on, unlit by CODE:2E952 at t=142.614)
name       CODE:2E82F LAMP_OFF      ; the lamp of the slot-15 record [CODE:0008] off for the player
comment    CODE:2E82F the light state at +4 of the record at [CODE:0008], for the player CODE:0038: its bit in byte +0 cleared, byte +2 bits 0 and 1 cleared (not blinking), +1 FFh, +3 and +4 0
name       CODE:2EF7A LIGHTS_STEP   ; the light states of header slot 14's groups, a frame
comment    CODE:2EF7A once a frame (CODE:2B49A) along the groups of header slot 14 (state+28DEh; the place state+16AEh, the light's number state+16ACh), starting groups until 20h lights are visited in the call, and at most 8 lights drawn in it (a group cut off by that is visited again from its start in the next call): a blinking light (+2 bit 1) counts +3 down and below 0 inverts +1 and reloads +3 from +4, so the blink is counted in visits, not frames; a light is shown when +1 is not 0 and its byte +0 or +5 has the current player's bit (state+0D72h), drawn on (CODE:28FBA) or off (CODE:28FF8) when that differs from state+16B2h+number, and not drawn with +2 bit 2. A group whose lights were all shown and none blinking gets, unless its byte +4 has bit 1 (the groups with no stream in the modules), bit 0 set, once: its event stream +6 to EVENT_QUEUE and CODE:2EF17 (a word 10h and the group to the list at state+1822h, bit 0 of each light's byte +2 set; not followed). Then, once a press of a flipper key (state+2A7Bh, 2A7Ch; the latch state+2A7Ah), each group of the zero-ended list stored backwards before header slot 14's first pointer gets its lights' bytes +0 turned one place: each light takes the next one's, the last the first's (the lane change, presumably). That list holds one group in tables 2, 3 and 4 (96E4h and 8FD6h with 3 lights, 91B0h with 4), none in table 1
; the drop targets (2026-09-29, read from the code and the four modules'
; objects; no run made for it). An object of type 1 (word +0) of the
; 0C0h dwords at header slot 4 (state+28B6h, zeros between): its number
; +44h, down +0Bh (FFh), a light state +2, its sound record +6, its bank
; +22h, the next of its bank +1Eh, the picture's place +2Eh, +32h, its
; picture pair +36h, a width +42h (0: the picture's), the mask +3Ah at
; the byte +26h, bit shift +3Eh, of the level +2Ah picks (1: header slot
; 1's map, else slot 7's). A bank: the first target +0, no raising
; with bit 0 of +4, points before +16h (12 BCD digits), an event stream
; +16h. Found this way: table 1 one bank of 2 (5128h), table 4 three
; (3, 3, 2 targets: 472Ch, 49AAh, 4AA2h; 472Ch with bit 0), tables 2
; and 3 none
name       CODE:28E5D DROP_SET      ; the state [CODE:0020] of the drop target [CODE:0000] into the table CODE:288DC (8 bytes by its number: the state, the state drawn, the object)
name       CODE:28EA6 DROPS_DRAW    ; each frame (CODE:298C5, after BALLS_STEP) the 64h entries of CODE:288DC
comment    CODE:28EA6 an entry whose state differs from the one drawn: the picture +36h x 2, less 1 when the state is odd (from drops.mgl, the "Droptargets (Gfx)" load at CODE:28D64), drawn at +2Eh, +32h (CODE:290D7), and its mask put into the level's map (DROP_MASK)
name       CODE:2942C DROP_MASK     ; the drop target's mask (masks.mgl) cleared from the level's map (a state not 0) or set in it (0); the map a bit a pixel, 2Ah bytes (336 pixels) a line; four routines by the width 10h, 18h, 20h, 30h; the ball's collisions with the map, presumably, not followed
name       CODE:2C7FC OBJECT_HITS   ; each frame (CODE:2B4B9) for each ball in play (byte +9 0): its word +6Ch (not negative) picks an object in the table at its +60h (header slot 4 or 10, by the level: CODE:2C414, 2C467), handled by the object's type (word +0, switch at CODE:2C8BC: 0 OBJECT_TYPE0, 1 DROP_HIT, 2 OBJECT_TYPE2); +6Ch is set by BALL_COLLIDE (a surface number 20h and above, less 20h)
name       CODE:2C8C2 OBJECT_TYPE0  ; [CODE:0000] the object, [CODE:0020]'s low word its index: below 20h only when its timer (byte +2) is 0, then set to 6 (OBJECT_TIMERS counts it down); with a light state at +4 the player's bit set in it: when it was set already the light flashed 8 times (LIGHT_QUEUE) and the points of the record at +0Ch to the score only (SCORE_ADD from +1Ah), else flashed 0Ch times and, as without a light, the record's points (TAKE_PAY from +12h); the object's record +8 (RECORD_DISPATCH), the record's event stream +1Ah and the object's +10h (EVENT_QUEUE). Run 2026-10-01, table 1, blind flipper play: index 1 at the first entry, the light branch with 0Ch; the light already set, an index of 20h and above and a running timer not run
name       CODE:2CB03 OBJECT_TYPE2  ; [CODE:0000] the object: when the slot-15 record at +2 is lit for the player (its byte +1), the ball's speed (+0Eh, +10h) set to the object's words +6, +8 and the record taken (RECORD_TAKE); not run
name       CODE:2C9D4 DROP_HIT      ; a drop target hit by a ball
comment    CODE:2C9D4 the player's bit (state+0D72h) set in byte +0 of the light state +2, the bank's points (+0Eh..+15h, TAKE_PAY), the record +6 to CODE:9F2C (as a record of type 2 through RECORD_DISPATCH), down (+0Bh FFh) and queued for DROP_SET (state+2A60h); when every target of the bank is down: the bank's stream +16h to EVENT_QUEUE, and unless its +4 bit 0 is set the bank onto the stack state+2AD0h to be raised (DROPS_RAISE_STEP). Run 2026-09-29, table 1, blind play: target 5188h hit at t=205.128 and again one frame later, 5142h at 209.887 and 209.901; the bank's stream (5128h +16h: light 51E0h, block 5218h) queued at both of the last two, 51E0h lit; so a hit is handled in two frames running, presumably while the ball's +6Ch stays
name       CODE:30799 DROPS_RAISE_STEP ; each frame (CODE:30784 from CODE:2B49A): with no bank waiting, one taken from the stack state+2AD0h and 64h frames set (state+2AD8h); when they run out every target of the bank is up (+0Bh 0) and queued for DROP_SET
name       CODE:3086D DROPS_QUEUE_STEP ; each frame: one entry of the queue at state+2A60h (a word, 1: a drop target, whose +0Bh goes to DROP_SET)
name       CODE:2A39A DROPS_UP_ALL  ; at the game start (GAME_PHASE 2, CODE:2A976): every drop target up (DROP_SET at once), the stacks at state+2AD0h, 2A60h and 2A64h (the holes') set empty
name       CODE:2A421 DROPS_UP_BALL ; at the next ball (CODE:2BCC0): every drop target up but those with bit 0 of +4
; the holes' eject (2026-09-29, read from the code; no run made for it).
; A hole (the object of a type-4 zone): bit 1 of +0 set by opcode 18h
; (the ball out at the second hole, +34h), byte +1 the ball held (its
; number + 1 in state+C107Ah's table), the count +4, where the ball comes
; out +6, +8, its speed +0Ah, +0Ch, the level +0Eh (0 or 1), a sound
; record +10h, an object of the table CODE:285BC +30h (drawn by CODE:28E7B)
name       CODE:30996 HOLE_EJECT_STEP ; each frame (CODE:30784 from CODE:2B49A): the hole ejecting (state+2A68h), else the next from the stack state+2A64h
comment    CODE:30368 host vector +18h: the binary word in [CODE:0020] as decimal digits (BCD, each nonzero nibble from the tables at CODE:30585, 305A5, 305C5) ending at [CODE:0000]; uses CODE:0004, 0008, 0028, 002C as work cells, so a module that keeps a pointer in CODE:0004 loses it here: [CODE:0004] is left at CODE:30585 or 305A5 + 2 x (the highest nonzero nibble) - 2. Table 1's shooting game reads its state through CODE:0004 after this call (module 9D80h), so its 25-hit test reads a byte of these tables instead (not FFh for any count 1..29, read from the image; run 2026-09-29 with 26 hits: the other branch taken; docs/HANDOFF.md, "Table 1's shooting game when the lives run out")
comment    CODE:30996 with bit 1 the second hole (+34h) stands in for the hole in what follows but the count. A count below 0 counts up and at 0 puts the ball out at once (CODE:30C5C). A count above 0 counts down: at 3Ch the ball is put out (CODE:30CAD), below 32h every 8th frame the sound record +10h (CODE:9F2C) and each frame the object +30h drawn in state count AND 4 (CODE:28E7B: it flickers every 4 frames), at 0 the hole is done (state+2A68h 0; without bit 1 the program's own record CODE:100E8, a sound presumably, through RECORD_DISPATCH), its ball no longer held (bit 7 of the ball's byte +1). Without bit 1 the sound record is read from [CODE:0004]+10h, and CODE:0004 then still holds what DROPS_QUEUE_STEP left there (state+2A60h's place), not the hole: a slip. Run 2026-09-29, table 1 (hole module 4F18h, both ejects at t=149.37 and 172.13): [CODE:0004] was F920h, the queue's empty end, at all 14 reads, and CODE:F930 is 0 (the queue grows down from F920h, nothing writes above it), so nothing sounds and that frame's draw is skipped as well (the JE to the RET); the hole's own +10h is module 11BBFh, a type-2 record. With three or more entries left in the queue the read would land in the queue's entries, a pointer of their bytes to CODE:9F2C (read, not run)
comment    CODE:30BD6 the next hole from the stack state+2A64h (opcode 8, 18h): its count +4 is 4Ch (76 frames) when the hole that puts the ball out has an object at +30h, else FFCEh (-50: 50 frames, no picture). Run 2026-09-29, table 1: 4Ch twice (t=148.980, 171.732), the ball out 0.223 and 0.227 s later (16 frames); FFCEh not seen
name       CODE:30CFB HOLE_BALL_OUT
comment    CODE:30CFB the ball out: its words +12h, +14h = +6, +8 (and shifted by 0Ah into its dwords +1Eh, +22h), the high bytes of its words +0Eh, +10h cleared and +0Ah, +0Ch added, then onto level +0Eh as zone type 3 (0: CODE:2C414) or type 2 (1: CODE:2C467) do
; the display language (the same way; opcodes 4, 5, 0Bh, 11h, 12h, 15h..17h
; are in none of the modules' streams the tool finds)
comment    CODE:2F35C the display queue's runner: waits while state+2A40h (frames) counts down, and after opcode 7 (state+2A3Ch) while an animation of opcode 1 runs (state+2A50h), then while state+2A3Eh counts down; else one command of the running stream (state+2A2Eh, else the next of the ring at [state+2A2Ah], filled by CODE:2FEDB) by the table at CODE:2F621 (record n at +4n, as CODE:2D18F; commands from +6, the position word at +4); with none queued, the background stream (state+2A58h) runs to its end at once (CODE:2F555)
comment    CODE:2FEDB a display stream to the queue: word +0 bit 0 set: it becomes the background stream (state+2A58h); else by its bytes +2, +3 against the running one's (state+2A3Ah, 2A3Bh): +2 lower, or equal and +3 lower, dropped; +2 higher or negative, or both equal: the queue emptied, the displays cleared (CODE:2FBA8, BA9B) and it queued; +2 equal and +3 higher: queued behind
comment    CODE:2F9CF display opcode 1 (an animation, five words): state+2A50h = it (a wait of opcode 7 waits for it first); its +6..+0Eh from the words (the first shifted right by 4 and doubled), +12h from +22h, +10h and +16h cleared; played by ANIMS_STEP; state+2A50h also cleared when DISPLAY_QUEUE empties the queue (CODE:2FF7A)
comment    CODE:2F7A5 display opcode 2: both display buffers cleared (CODE:2FBA8)
comment    CODE:2FB17 display opcode 3 (a text record): through CODE:27783 (host vector +14h, docs/bpc-module.md)
comment    CODE:2FBA4 display opcodes 4, 15h, 16h, 17h (a dword each): a RET
comment    CODE:2FB2C display opcode 5 (a pointer, four words): the word before the pointer, its bytes swapped, AND 0FFFh, shown as a number (CODE:1010A), the words its layout (CODE:002C..0038)
comment    CODE:2F712 display opcode 6 (a pointer, four words): the packed-BCD number that ends at the pointer shown through CODE:275E4 (host vector +10h), the words its layout (CODE:002C..0038)
comment    CODE:2FB6F display opcode 7 (a word): waits the word times FRAME_RATE (state+50h) in frames (state+2A3Eh, 2A3Ch)
comment    CODE:2FA88 display opcode 8 (four words): the current player's score (the record at state+0D76h, its +8) shown through CODE:275E4; the third word 1 becomes 3 when the record's word +0 is not 0 (not followed)
comment    CODE:2F812 display opcode 9 (a pointer, four words): the current player's word (at the pointer plus twice the player, less 2), AND 0FFFh, shown as a number (CODE:1015E)
comment    CODE:2F7B1 display opcode 0Ah (a word): waits that many frames (state+2A40h)
comment    CODE:2F7CA display opcode 0Bh (a code address): called, with [CODE:0000] = it
comment    CODE:2F68D display opcode 0Ch (an animation, five words, the fifth not read): as opcode 1 into state+2A5Ch, without the wait; nothing when it is the one there already
; the animations (2026-09-29, read from the code and the four modules'
; display streams; no run made for it). An animation record of the
; module: +0 the next played beside it (0 in every record opcodes 1 and
; 0Ch name), +6 the place ((word >> 4) x 2, times 4 the byte offset in
; the buffer), +0Eh repeats (the fifth word: 0 in most uses, up to 9),
; +10h/+11h a step every +11h+1 calls (1..3 in the modules), +12h the
; frames left, +16h the frame's data, +1Ah, +1Eh its width and height,
; +22h the frame count, +24h the first frame's number in
; data\s00n\anims\allanims.mgl ("Manglade Anims", CODE:2791F)
name       CODE:27A0E ANIMS_STEP    ; a step of the display's animations, a call a frame after DISPLAY_RUN (CODE:2A690, 2B83D, 2B95A, 2BA0A)
comment    CODE:27A0E the list at state+2A50h (opcode 1; last state+2A54h), each record a step: the next frame drawn (ANIM_FRAME), and after +22h of them it starts again while +0Eh counts down, else it leaves the list (its +0 cleared; the list's head then 0: DISPLAY_RUN's wait of opcode 7 ends). A record still counting +10h ends the call. With the list empty, the animation of opcode 0Ch (state+2A5Ch) plays the same way but starts again for ever; it is set back to its first frame while the list plays or a display stream runs (state+2A2Eh), and then not drawn
name       CODE:27C2A ANIM_FRAME    ; one frame into the 160-byte-a-line buffer (1400h bytes, 160 x 32, cleared to FCh by CODE:27CEC; the dot display, presumably)
comment    CODE:27C2A a new start (+16h 0) takes frame +24h (1 when not below the file's count, its dword 0), its header words width, height, count to +1Ah, +1Eh, +22h (and +12h); a data byte up to 4 is a pixel of colour FCh + byte (4: 00h), above 4 skips byte - 4 pixels; the frames follow one another in the file (+16h goes on past the one drawn)
comment    CODE:2F7AB display opcode 0Dh: one display buffer cleared (CODE:27259)
comment    CODE:2F982 display opcode 0Eh (four words): as opcode 5 with the word at state+2A6Eh: the seconds left of the mode stream's wait (CODE:2CD3C)
comment    CODE:2F79F display opcode 0Fh: the other display buffer cleared (CODE:27CEC)
comment    CODE:2FB02 display opcode 10h (a record): through CODE:3007A (by its type: an audio record, a slot-31 record, ...)
comment    CODE:2FA55 display opcode 11h: a RET
comment    CODE:2F755 display opcode 12h (four words): as opcode 8 with the player record's +10h
comment    CODE:2FAE9 display opcode 13h (a word): the loop count state+2A4Eh (opcode 14h)
comment    CODE:2FA56 display opcode 14h (a position): state+2A4Eh counted down; unless it is 0, a jump to the position: a loop
comment    CODE:2F80C display opcode 18h: DAC colours FCh..FFh from the second set (CODE:BAB6)
comment    CODE:2F9C9 display opcode 19h: DAC colours FCh..FFh from the first set (CODE:BA9B)
comment    CODE:2F7DE display opcode 1Ah (a text record, a word): shown (CODE:27783) when the word AND the word at CODE:BAD4 is not 0; CODE:BAD4 is counted up by DRV_TICK (CODE:B99C, the sound driver's command-0Eh routine; about 70 a second in a run, once a frame): blinking text
; the zones' types (the switch at CODE:2C3DD; the object at the zone's +0Ah)
comment    CODE:2C59C zone type 0: as type 1 (from CODE:2C61F), first, when state+0D2Fh is set, the event stream of header slot 27 (state+2912h) or 28 (2916h) to EVENT_QUEUE by whether state+0E38h equals state+0D36h (not followed): a skill shot, presumably
comment    CODE:2C4B5 zone type 1: on entry the object's points (from +1Eh; through CODE:2FD11 from +26h instead when the record at +0Ah has the player's bit already), its +2 through CODE:3007A, its +6 (an event stream) to EVENT_QUEUE
comment    CODE:2C462 zone type 2: the ball's +50h..+64h from header slots 6..11 (state+28BEh), byte +8 FFh: onto the other level, presumably
comment    CODE:2C40F zone type 3: the ball's +50h..+64h from header slots 0..5 (state+28A6h), byte +8 0
name       CODE:2C719 ZONE_TYPE4
comment    CODE:2C719 zone type 4, a hole: unless the ball is held (bit 7 of its byte +1), when the hole's byte +1 is 0 it holds the ball (its number to byte +1), the points before +2Ch (CODE:2FBBF), the main program's record at CODE:100CE through CODE:3007A, the event stream at +14h to EVENT_QUEUE
words      CODE:2DA0A 1C CODE      ; PUSH [EBX*4+2DA0A] at CODE:2DA02 after PUSH 2DA09h, then RET: by the word at [[CODE:0008]+2Ch] (0 not taken); 28 up to the first target (a RET at CODE:2DA7A)
words      CODE:2CD10 0B CODE      ; its address put in [CODE:0010] (CODE:2BEDC, 2D04D, 2DBD3) before calls into the table module: its host vector (docs/bpc-module.md), +14h (CODE:27783) draws a text record, +1Ch is EVENT_QUEUE (checked 2026-09-29: table 1's and 2's arguments there are event streams), the others not checked one by one

; the keyboard (runs of 2026-09-29 with doskit's -rwatch on CODE:D984)
code       CODE:A076 KBD_IRQ       ; installed at CODE:A03B with INT 93h AH=4 BL=1 (presumably IRQ1's vector; the old one saved with AH=3); run: entered on each key event, CS=000C
ds         CODE:A08E-A10B CODE     ; DS from CODE:A10B (the selector made at CODE:A323 from DS); run: its writes land at CODE's addresses (KEY_DOWN below)
name       CODE:D984 KEY_DOWN     ; 256 bytes, FFh while the key is down: the scan code, +80h after an E0h prefix (run: +2Ah FFh on Left Shift down, 00h on its release)
name       CODE:DA84 KEY_TOGGLE    ; the same index, the byte inverted on each press
name       CODE:A016 LAST_KEY      ; the last scan code pressed (without 80h); also stored at CODE:CC2F
name       CODE:A01D KEY_E0        ; FFh after an E0h prefix
name       CODE:A2C7 KEY_RELEASED  ; FFh after a release: a press of Space (39h) or Alt (38h, E0 38h) counts only then (no typematic repeat for them, presumably); a press dropped so leaves KEY_E0 as it is, so after a dropped E0 38h (Right Alt) the next key counts as an E0 key (from the code, not seen in a run)
; reads of KEY_DOWN through the record at [CODE:0014] (CB3Eh in the runs:
; KEY_DOWN is its field E46h); the field offsets stay numbers
comment    CODE:144BA Space (KEY_DOWN+39h) pushes the word at [ESI+0D48h] up by 258h a frame to 3E8h, then clears the key; down by C8h without it: presumably a nudge (upward), not checked
num        CODE:144BA
num        CODE:14520
comment    CODE:145A0 Left Alt (KEY_DOWN+38h) and Right Alt (+B8h) move the word at [ESI+0D46h] down / up by 258h to -3E8h / 3E8h: presumably nudges left and right, not checked; Space, Left Alt, Right Alt set bits 0, 1, 2 of [ESI+2A77h] on a new press
num        CODE:145A0
num        CODE:1460A
num        CODE:1461C
num        CODE:14686
comment    CODE:14757 the flippers (run: Left Shift held, the left flipper up in the picture): left = Left Shift or Left Ctrl (KEY_DOWN+2Ah, +1Dh) to [ESI+2A7Bh], right = Right Shift or Right Ctrl (+36h, E0 1Dh) to [ESI+2A7Ch]
num        CODE:14757
num        CODE:1475D
num        CODE:14769
num        CODE:1476F
comment    CODE:2F300 Enter (KEY_DOWN+1Ch) launches the waiting ball (run: F1, then Enter: the ball moves; Down, held 3 s, is read by no one): the index at [[ESI+2906h]] cleared, 1770h taken from the word +10h of the object at [ESI+1076h+index*4] (presumably its speed, upward)
num        CODE:2F306
num        CODE:2F315
comment    CODE:2A7FD in the attract mode: Esc (KEY_DOWN+1) to CODE:2A8AB; F1..F8 (+3Bh..+42h, the field at [ESI+0E81h]) or keypad Enter (E0 1Ch) set [ESI+8Eh] to 2 and add the key's number (1..8; keypad Enter 1) to [ESI+0D70h] (run: F1 starts a game, "PLAYERS 1"; the others not tried)

; offsets among the 32-bit immediates (2026-09-29): ptrscan.py (49) and a
; throwaway scan of every 4-byte immediate from 100h to the image's end that
; was no label (642 besides branches), each sorted by how its register is
; used next and by eye. Numbers left as they are: counts in ECX, sizes in
; EBX for INT 92h, strides (C4E0h, 1500h, 5C0h), offsets in other selectors
; (video memory after OUT 3C4h; ES/DS/FS from INT 93h AH=5, CODE:130F, A117,
; 634A/634C, 3B4B: INFODATA_SEL, see CODE:4532) and a CD time (CODE:35DE8). ES from CODE:A10B, 131D, 635E
; is taken for CODE (copies of DS, presumably the start-up alias). Lengths of
; checksummed stretches (ECX before CODE:4CE8/4CF2/7438/7441) stay numbers:
; the kit has no label differences.
comment    CODE:523B the dword at 290FBh+7CBh = CODE:298C6 is the immediate of MOV EBX,14DE2h; CALL EBX at CODE:298C5: overwritten here with [[CODE:5DCB]+13h]+[CODE:55E3] (the variable the dead copy-protection pieces write) when the byte at CODE:037C is 1. CODE:037C is the 0 before the text CODE:0372 prints and no instruction in the image names it but the CMP here; runs of 2026-09-29 (the chooser left for table 1 and by Esc): CODE:523B not reached, CODE:298C6 written once, by the loader at t=2.28, and CODE:298C5 called 14DE2h once a frame. Presumably the protection's switch, dead in this release as its pieces are; the base 290FBh left a number
; the chooser's Info page and the hidden greetings page (2026-09-29, from
; the code and runs on Linux; hints below CODE:4532)
name       CODE:3B4B INFODATA_SEL  ; the selector INT 94h AH=1 gives for chooser\infodata.mgl (stored by the POPs at CODE:4FD6 and 76EE), freed with INT 92h AH=5; DS for INFO_PAGE's text
name       CODE:3B4D TINYFONT_SEL  ; the same for chooser\tinyfont.fnt (CODE:4F85, 76AD); FS for the text routines, the character widths at FS:[4 x character + 2] (CODE:41D4)
name       CODE:3B58 TEXT_POS      ; the next character of the page being written (430Ah + an offset in INFODATA.MGL, or 46AFh in CODE)
name       CODE:1538 KEY_HISTORY   ; the last four scan codes pressed, the newest in the low byte (CODE:340A); 0F3A2A1Dh, Tab, Caps Lock, Left Shift, Left Ctrl in that order, opens GREETINGS_PAGE as the menu starts (CODE:506C) and, checked each frame of CHOOSER_WAIT (CODE:3943), sets WAIT_END, so the four keys alone bring the page up. Run 2026-09-29: the four keys at t=106..107.5 after Space at 100 (the menu on screen), the dword 0F3A2A1Dh at 108.0, CODE:505C and GREETINGS_PAGE at 108.53
code       CODE:4504 INFO_PAGE     ; the menu's Info entry (called at CODE:509B when MENU_INFO is set): the page of MENU_ROW from INFODATA.MGL (see CODE:4532), with a picture, the table's high scores and "Press ESC to exit."; waits for ESC_KEY (PAGE_KEYS), fades out (CODE:461C) and returns to the menu (runs 2026-09-29: the first page, Law 'N Justice; row 2, Extreme Sports, at t=111.56, Esc at 118, the menu loop again at 118.73 with the cursor on row 2)
name       CODE:46AF GREETINGS_TEXT ; the greetings page's text (FrontLine Design's greetings and a note on the program's size), ended by 0; written by GREETINGS_PAGE
code       CODE:4871 GREETINGS_PAGE ; the text before it (CODE:46AF) on the chooser's screen in the small font; reached only by KEY_HISTORY (run 2026-09-29, the page on screen from t=108.5)
name       CODE:18F8 MENU_ROWS     ; 4, the menu's rows (the tables); MENU_ROW stays below it
name       CODE:18F9 MENU_ROW      ; the menu's row, the table: Down and Up (CODE:3551, 356E), F1..F4 (CODE:35F8) set it; set to 0 only by CODE:505C and CHOOSER_WAIT, so it is kept across INFO_PAGE; the table number in AL at CODE:526D (FFh on Esc). Runs 2026-09-29: 0, 1, 2 at Down at t=108, 109; F3 at 108 set 2 and table 3 (Extreme Sports) came up
name       CODE:18FB MENU_INFO     ; the menu's column: 1 Info (Right, CODE:3582), 0 the table (Left, CODE:358E; F1..F4); read after MENU_LOOP in CODE:505C
name       CODE:18FC MENU_ON       ; 1 in MENU_LOOP, 0 in CHOOSER_WAIT: only then Enter, Space and F1..F4 choose (CODE:359A, 35F8)
name       CODE:18FE MENU_FADE     ; 1 while the screen fades out to leave (Esc, a choice); MENU_KEYS takes no key then, and CODE:3325 sets MENU_DONE when the fade (CODE:132B) is at 0
name       CODE:18FF ESC_KEY       ; Esc seen (scan code 1: MENU_KEYS at CODE:350F, PAGE_KEYS at 3489); leaves INFO_PAGE and GREETINGS_PAGE (cleared there), else leaves the chooser for DOS (CODE:50A9, 5198, AL=FFh)
name       CODE:1904 WAIT_END      ; set by Esc, Enter and Space (MENU_KEYS; F1..F4 are dropped while MENU_ON is 0, CODE:35F8, run 2026-09-29: F1 at 130 and 132 left CHOOSER_WAIT running) and KEY_HISTORY (CODE:3943): CODE:3849 then blanks the chooser's caption (CODE:1728) and counts CODE:1900 to 4, which ends CHOOSER_WAIT
name       CODE:1916 MENU_DONE     ; set when a fade after MENU_FADE is done (CODE:3325); ends CHOOSER_WAIT and MENU_LOOP
code       CODE:3465 PAGE_KEYS     ; the keys of INFO_PAGE and GREETINGS_PAGE from the ring at CODE:1906: only Esc counts (ESC_KEY), the rest are dropped. Runs 2026-09-29: Esc left the Info page at t=118 and the greetings page at 112, the menu loop again 0.7 s later
code       CODE:3492 MENU_KEYS     ; the chooser's keys from the ring at CODE:1906, one a frame: Esc, Down, Up, Right, Left, Enter and Space, F1..F4 (see the names above); the rest dropped
code       CODE:38C6 CHOOSER_WAIT  ; the chooser's backdrop (the turning shapes) with the captions of CODE:1898 in turn and no list, until WAIT_END or MENU_DONE (runs 2026-09-29: from t=104.21 after Space at 100 ended the credits; Enter at 106.01 ended it)
code       CODE:3969 MENU_LOOP     ; the table list and Info, a frame a turn, until MENU_DONE (runs 2026-09-29: from t=106.76; again after INFO_PAGE and GREETINGS_PAGE)
name       CODE:1890 CAPTION       ; the offset of the caption record drawn over the chooser's backdrop, its routine at +18h or +1Eh on alternate frames (CODE:32EE, CODE:132A); from CAPTIONS in CHOOSER_WAIT, from the three tables below in MENU_LOOP (CODE:364F)
name       CODE:1894 CAPTION_NEXT  ; the next entry of CAPTIONS (CODE:3883)
name       CODE:1898 CAPTIONS      ; 11 dwords, offsets of caption records, then FFFFFFFFh: CODE:1704, 174C, 1794, 17B8, 17DC, 1800, 1824, 1848, 1770, 186C, 1728 (Pinball Illusions; Concept and Design; PC Version; Programming, twice; Graphics; Music and Original Amiga Code; Production; Licensed by; Press Space Bar for Table Menu, Press ESC to quit; nothing). Left numbers: the kit's words hint with CODE as target would take the zero-filled records for code
name       CODE:18C8 MENU_PICS     ; 4 offsets of caption records, the list with MENU_ROW boxed (CODE:1554, 1578, 159C, 15C0; left numbers as CAPTIONS)
name       CODE:18D8 MENU_INFO_PICS ; the same with Info boxed (CODE:15E4, 1608, 162C, 1650)
name       CODE:18E8 MENU_PICS_NOBOX ; the same with no box (CODE:1674, 1698, 16BC, 16E0), taken while MENU_BLINK is 1
name       CODE:18FA MENU_BLINK    ; flipped each time the backdrop's scroll wraps (CODE:2575), so the menu's box blinks (run 2026-09-29: the list at t=117 without its box)
code       CODE:302E CAPTION_BUILD ; a caption record at EBX from the layout at ESI (the layouts CODE:1AE6..226E): a list of commands, FFh ends it. 0 y text 0: text from the left edge (leading spaces place it); 1 y text 0: text centred on x 98h (widths from CODE:55E7); 2 x1(word) y x2(word): a horizontal line; 3 x(word) y1 y2: a vertical line; y is a line of 2Eh bytes. Drawn into two bitmaps at FS (CODE:131B, the second at +2E04h), then six routines made by CODE:2E35 whose far pointers fill the record's 24h bytes (six selectors freed by CODE:28CF)
code       CODE:39C8 CAPTIONS_MAKE ; every caption record made by CAPTION_BUILD from its layout, 64 KiB taken by INT 92h AH=6 first (CODE:153C)
; the chooser's start, CODE:4CFB to CHOOSER (2026-09-30, a -trace of the run from CODE:4CFB)
name       CODE:131D CHOOSER_DS    ; DS (1Ch) kept by CODE:4CFB
code       CODE:33B8 KBD_INSTALL   ; IRQ 1's vector kept at KBD_OLD (INT 93h AH=3 BL=1; run: 0030:00004152), set to CODE:340A (AH=4), INT 93h AH=9 BL=1 (not looked into), IRQ 1 unmasked
name       CODE:152E KBD_OLD       ; IRQ 1's vector before KBD_INSTALL (offset dword, selector at CODE:1532)
code       CODE:23CA CHOOSER_MODE  ; after mode 0Dh: sequencer 1 89h, the CRTC's timing (304 pixels, 2Eh bytes a line: CR 1 25h, CR 13h 17h, CR 9 41h, ...), misc bits 6-7 set, attribute registers 0-15 to 0-15; CODE:191A 1 (the start address from CODE:1323 at each retrace, CODE:4C93)
code       CODE:29D2 CHOOSER_DAC   ; while CODE:132B is not negative: DAC 0-16 (33h bytes) from CODE:13A4
code       CODE:24AF SPLIT_SET     ; the line compare from CX less 1 (bit 8 from CH bit 0 into CR 7; CR 9 bit 6 cleared); reached from CODE:4DB6 with CX 1BDh (run)
code       CODE:24F8 CHOOSER_VIDEO ; CHOOSER_VSEL from INT 93h AH=5
name       CODE:130F CHOOSER_VSEL  ; video memory's selector (48h)
code       CODE:2503 VIDEO_CLEAR   ; all four planes, 10000h bytes, cleared
code       CODE:2613 SCROLL_INIT   ; CODE:131F, 1321, 1323 E60h (the start addresses of the backdrop's scroll, presumably; not followed), CODE:1329 3
code       CODE:2810 MENUCHAR_INIT ; chooser\menuchar.rix loaded unless CHOOSER_LOADED (the run: loaded, by CHOOSER_LOAD); CHAR_STRIDE and CHAR_OFFS from it
name       CODE:150A CHAR_STRIDE   ; menuchar.rix's word +4 shifted right 3
name       CODE:140A CHAR_OFFS     ; 128 words: a character's glyph in menuchar.rix, 3Ah and then each glyph's height * CHAR_STRIDE * 4 on
name       CODE:55E7 CHAR_TAB      ; 128 entries of 3 bytes: the advance in pixels, the height in lines, the line (less 1) the glyph starts at
code       CODE:299B WRITE_MODE1   ; GC 5 01h (write mode 1, the latches), map mask 0Fh
code       CODE:29B0 READ_MODE1    ; GC 3 10h (function OR), GC 2 0Fh, GC 5 08h (read mode 1, write mode 0)
code       CODE:2FE3 VIDEO_TOP_SET ; 26h bytes of FFh at video memory 0 (function OR: all four planes set there)
code       CODE:3397 BITMAP_ALLOC  ; INT 92h AH=7 5C08h bytes (name CODE:226F): BITMAP_SEL
code       CODE:33AC BITMAP_FREE   ; INT 92h AH=5 BITMAP_SEL
name       CODE:131B BITMAP_SEL    ; CAPTION_BUILD's two bitmaps of 2E04h bytes (2Eh a line, a bit a pixel)
name       CODE:153C GEN_BUF       ; CAPTIONS_MAKE's 64 KiB (INT 92h AH=6: a linear address, run: FDA3D0h), where GEN_CODE builds a routine before its copy
code       CODE:2CE3 CHAR_DRAW     ; character AL of menuchar.rix into both bitmaps at bit EBX (a line is 170h bits), EBX moved on by its advance: each glyph line's two words, bits in both to the first, then shifted right by EBX's low 3 bits
code       CODE:3013 BITMAP_CLEAR  ; BITMAP_SEL's 5C08h bytes cleared
code       CODE:31BB BITMAP_FRAME  ; a bitmap's frame: its first line all set, then 223 lines with the left bit and the 26h-th byte's low bit
code       CODE:2E35 GEN_CODE      ; a caption routine made in GEN_BUF from the bitmap at ESI and the one at [GEN_OTHER] (EDI), E0h lines of 26h bytes: for a set byte a latch read at SI (GEN_LATCH) and a byte write of it at DI (GEN_BYTE), for a byte set only in the other (in lines while CH > 20h) a latch read and MOV [DI+d],BH (GEN_BH); every 32 lines ADD DI,5C0h and SI anew (GEN_SI); RETF (66h CBh); copied into a new block (INT 92h AH=4, name CODE:2F13; INT 93h AH=14h CX 9Ah); the record at EBX: dword 0, the selector
code       CODE:2F14 GEN_CODE2     ; the same with byte writes only (GEN_BYTE for a byte set in either bitmap), no latch reads
name       CODE:2E31 GEN_OTHER     ; GEN_CODE's second bitmap's offset, moved on 5C0h every 32 lines
code       CODE:2D72 GEN_LATCH     ; MOV AL,[SI+EBP] (8A 04 / 8A 44 d8 / 8A 84 d16)
code       CODE:2D9B GEN_BYTE      ; MOV BYTE PTR [DI+EBX],DL (C6 05 / C6 45 d8 / C6 85 d16)
code       CODE:2DCD GEN_BH        ; MOV [DI+EBX],BH (88 3D / 88 7D d8 / 88 BD d16)
code       CODE:2DF6 GEN_SI        ; MOV SI,ES:[150Ch+2*DH] and ADD SI,ES:[151Ch+2*DH] (26h 8Bh 36h, 26h 03h 36h, 16-bit offsets), DH counted
code       CODE:2E23 GEN_NEXT      ; ADD DI,5C0h (81h C7h), then GEN_SI
code       CODE:3849 CAPTION_STEP  ; in CHOOSER_WAIT: the next of CAPTIONS (at the backdrop's scroll, CODE:1901, CODE:18FD); after WAIT_END the empty caption, then CODE:1900 counted to 4. Run 2026-09-29, no keys: a new caption every 5.05 s from t=109.63, the list round again at 165.86
code       CODE:36AE ATTRACT_START ; stage 1 of ATTRACT_STEP, 300 frames to go (CODE:1917, 1919), the first palette CODE:191B
code       CODE:36F4 ATTRACT_STEP  ; each frame: after 300 frames (CODE:1917) the backdrop's next palette, 33h bytes each from CODE:191B by the stage CODE:1919, faded in (CODE:132B); after stage 9 the next of three backdrops (CODE:1311 by CODE:132D) is set up (CODE:376A). Run 2026-09-29, no keys: stages 5.03 s apart from t=112.90 (blue cubes, then purple, ...), the crosses from 148.42
comment    CODE:505C the table menu's start (runs 2026-09-29: entered when CHOOSER_WAIT ends, t=106.76 with Enter at 106; Space at 100 only ends the credits); MENU_DONE set here means Esc in CHOOSER_WAIT, straight to CODE:50A9 and out: GREETINGS_PAGE when KEY_HISTORY asks for it, then the menu loop CODE:3969 and INFO_PAGE while CODE:18FB is set
comment    CODE:4FF9 the chooser (reached at t=97.6 in the runs); it ends at CODE:51D6 when a table is chosen (t=106.56, the CD stop there) or on Esc (t=101.11, the program then exits with 32): the sound driver's commands 5 and 0Bh, the selector in CODE:8138 freed, CD_STOP, a checksummed call
comment    CODE:50A9 a keyboard table by INT 93h AH=15h (a country code in AH:AL, presumably the keyboard's; not checked): BE and FR the AZERTY one at CODE:6023, the eight codes at CODE:50EE (HU, YU, SF, SG, CZ, SL, PL, GR) the QWERTZ one at CODE:5F22, else the QWERTY one at CODE:5E21 (the runs); copied upper-case to CODE:2B0A2, FFh for what is not a character
comment    CODE:29889 the frame step (runs: CODE:298C5 about 70 times a second on table 1): the four routines of the table at [CODE:2982E], a wait for CODE:BAD1 = FFh (set by the driver's command-0Fh routine CODE:B9B9), then 14DE2h, CODE:28EA6, 14C46, 156C4
comment    CODE:14DE2 each ball on the table (state+0D32h of them, the list at state+1046h) to CODE:0010, then CODE:14DD6 (CODE:26977, 269B0)
comment    CODE:4532 INFO_PAGE's text: 430Ah + the dword at +4 + 4 x [CODE:18F9] of INFODATA.MGL (the file starts with a count, 4, and one offset a page from +4, the first page's text at 430Ah + 14h), read with DS = INFODATA_SEL by CODE:41A8, 3FF3; so 430Ah is an offset in that file and stays a number. Run 2026-09-29 (Space at 100, Enter at 106, Right and Enter at 110, 111): INFO_PAGE at t=111.56, the Law 'N Justice page on screen. GREETINGS_PAGE (CODE:4886) stores 46AFh instead, read with DS unchanged by CODE:4197, 405E: the text in CODE
comment    CODE:33D0 a second handler through INT 93h AH=4 BL=1 (as KBD_IRQ at CODE:A05C): CODE:340A, reached by the ptr below
ds         CODE:3416-3450 CODE     ; DS from CODE:131D, a copy of DS (CODE:4CFB), presumably CODE
comment    CODE:340A a keyboard handler: the scan code (port 60h) into a ring of 16 bytes at CODE:1906 (index CODE:1903), shifted into KEY_HISTORY (CODE:1538); releases (80h and up) skipped; installed (CODE:33B8) with the chooser's table menu (run 2026-09-29: t=100.56, at Space)
ds         CODE:4C8C-4C92 CODE     ; DS from CODE:131D, as above
comment    CODE:4C85 the routine handed to the sound driver with command 0Eh at CODE:4CB6: counts the dword at CODE:1548 (presumably a timer tick, not checked)
comment    CODE:4C93 the routine handed with command 0Fh (ECX 1999h) at CODE:4CD1: the CRT start address (3D4h, 0Ch/0Dh) from CODE:1323 while CODE:191A is 1
; CHOOSER's first calls, CODE:4FF9 to CHOOSER_WAIT (2026-09-30; the targets from the run's memory at CODE:4FF9)
code       CODE:26FD CUBE_DRAW     ; the backdrop picture of the selector in AX (CUBE_SEL at CODE:500E) from its byte 3Ah into video memory 72A4h, each plane (map mask 1, 2, 4, 8) four times, rotated left by 0, 2, 4, 6 bits (32 lines of B8h bytes each, a line wrapped round; the picture's lines 2E0h bytes, B8h a plane); GC 3 0 (CODE:29C7)
code       CODE:4CB6 VSYNC_START   ; the sound driver's command 0Eh with CODE:4C85 (VSYNC_COUNT at each retrace) and 0Fh with CODE:4C93 and ECX 1999h (the start address a tenth of the display after the retrace, see NOSOUND.hints)
code       CODE:236A MUSIC_PLAY    ; the sound driver's command 1 with ECX 0Fh
code       CODE:4C85 VSYNC_CB      ; VSYNC_COUNT counted, DS from CHOOSER_DS
code       CODE:4C93 CRT_START_CB  ; while CRT_START_ON is 1: CRT_START to CRTC 0Ch/0Dh
name       CODE:1548 VSYNC_COUNT   ; a dword VSYNC_CB counts, once a retrace
name       CODE:1323 CRT_START     ; the start address CRT_START_CB sets (E60h from SCROLL_INIT)
name       CODE:191A CRT_START_ON  ; 1 from CHOOSER_MODE
; CHOOSER_WAIT's loop (CODE:38FD), read 2026-09-30
code       CODE:25BB FRAME_WAIT    ; waits for VSYNC_COUNT to change, counting FRAME_SPINS; with CODE:1534 1 (set at CODE:4FF1, the path that loads the chooser's files again) the driver's command 8 (BL 0, CL 0), and once command 0Dh gives 280Ah or more CODE:1534 0 and command 0Ch with EBX 100h (in the port since 2026-10-01)
name       CODE:154C FRAME_SPINS   ; a dword FRAME_WAIT counts while it waits; read by no instruction
code       CODE:2389 MUSIC_MIX     ; the sound driver's command 6
code       CODE:237C MUSIC_STOP    ; the sound driver's command 3
code       CODE:381C CRT_START_PICK ; CRT_START from SCROLL_TOP, or from SCROLL_SHOWN when ATTRACT_TIME is 1 and ATTRACT_STAGE 9 (the frame before a backdrop change)
code       CODE:32A2 CAPTION_DRAW  ; CAPTION's routine called with DS video memory, SI and BX 0, DI SCROLL_SHOWN: CAPTION_FLIP toggled, 0 the record's +0 (+0Ch with SCROLL_PHASE 2), FFh its +6 (+12h)
code       CODE:32EE CAPTION_DRAW2 ; the same with the record's +18h and +1Eh (the routines without latch reads), then MUSIC_MIX (CUBE_DRAW_WAIT)
name       CODE:132A CAPTION_FLIP  ; toggled by CAPTION_DRAW: which of a caption's two bitmaps is drawn
code       CODE:3325 PAL_FADE      ; while CH_FADE_LEVEL is not 0: CH_FADE_LEVEL less CH_FADE_STEP (not below 0), CHOOSER_PAL mixed from PAL_FROM (CH_FADE_LEVEL / 40h) and PAL_TO (the rest); at 0 with MENU_FADE MENU_DONE 1
name       CODE:132B CH_FADE_LEVEL ; 40h at a new palette, counted down to 0 by CH_FADE_STEP; CHOOSER_DAC sends CHOOSER_PAL while it is not negative
name       CODE:132C CH_FADE_STEP  ; PAL_FADE's step (2, 4, 1 on Esc)
name       CODE:13A4 CHOOSER_PAL   ; DAC 0-16 (33h bytes), CHOOSER_DAC's
name       CODE:1540 PAL_FROM      ; the palette faded from (an address)
name       CODE:1544 PAL_TO        ; the palette faded to
code       CODE:31DE LAG_SHIFT     ; each frame LAG_PIC's 8 words moved one on (LAG_PIC+0Eh's in at +0Ch, +0 dropped) and LAG_COL's too with LAG_STEP added (mod 80h): each 32-line band of a caption's routines reads the scroll of a frame later than the band above
name       CODE:150C LAG_COL       ; 8 words: the column a caption routine's band reads the backdrop at (MOV SI,ES:[150Ch+2n])
name       CODE:151C LAG_PIC       ; 8 words: added to it, the rotated copy's offset + 72A4h (ADD SI,ES:[151Ch+2n])
name       CODE:152C LAG_STEP      ; 0, or 4 on SCROLL_STEP's third frame
code       CODE:2C55 SCROLL_STEP   ; WAVE_POS on by 2 (mod 300h); SCROLL_PHASE counted 3, 2, 1: at 1 SCROLL_COL on, STRIP_DRAW at 2844h and SCROLL_NEXT4, else STRIP_DRAW at 2840h and SCROLL_NEXT
code       CODE:2BE8 STRIP_DRAW    ; the backdrop's 2Eh bytes by 32 lines at SCROLL_TOP + AX from column SCROLL_COL * 4 + WAVE_TAB[WAVE_POS] / 8 (mod 80h) of the copy SHIFT_OFFS[WAVE_TAB[WAVE_POS] AND 7]; LAG_COL+0Eh and LAG_PIC+0Eh from the same
code       CODE:29FF STRIP_COPY    ; CL columns of 32 latch copies: [SI+72A4h+B8h*k] to [DI+2Eh*k] and [DI+C9BCh+2Eh*k] (unrolled)
name       CODE:5289 WAVE_TAB      ; 300h bytes, 80h to DFh and back: a sine presumably (not plotted)
name       CODE:132E SHIFT_OFFS    ; 8 words: 0, 0, 1700h, 1700h, 2E00h, 2E00h, 4500h, 4500h, the rotated copies CUBE_DRAW made
name       CODE:1325 SCROLL_COL    ; 0..1Fh, on by one every third frame (COL_NEXT)
name       CODE:1327 WAVE_POS      ; WAVE_TAB's index, on by 2 a frame
name       CODE:1329 SCROLL_PHASE  ; 3, 2, 1 (SCROLL_STEP)
code       CODE:2980 COL_NEXT      ; SCROLL_COL on, 20h back to 0
code       CODE:259F SCROLL_NEXT   ; SCROLL_SHOWN from SCROLL_TOP, SCROLL_TOP on by 5C0h (32 lines), then SCROLL_WRAP
code       CODE:255A SCROLL_NEXT4  ; the same by 5C4h
code       CODE:2575 SCROLL_WRAP   ; SCROLL_TOP at 44A4h or more: less 3644h, CODE:18FD 0 and MENU_BLINK flipped; else CODE:18FD counted
name       CODE:131F SCROLL_TOP    ; the start address the backdrop is drawn at (E60h from SCROLL_INIT)
name       CODE:1321 SCROLL_SHOWN  ; SCROLL_TOP of the frame before, where the caption is drawn
name       CODE:1917 ATTRACT_TIME  ; ATTRACT_STEP's frames to the next stage (12Ch)
name       CODE:1919 ATTRACT_STAGE ; 1..9, 0 after a backdrop change
name       CODE:132D BACKDROP      ; 0..2: CUBE_SEL, TUBE_SEL, TORUS_SEL
code       CODE:263B CUBE_DRAW_WAIT ; CUBE_DRAW for a backdrop change, every 16 lines (map mask 0Fh) FRAME_WAIT, CRT_START from SCROLL_SHOWN and CAPTION_DRAW2
name       CODE:1902 KEY_READ      ; MENU_KEYS' index into the ring at CODE:1906 (low 4 bits); CODE:1903 the handler's
name       CODE:1900 CAPTION_OUT   ; counted by CAPTION_STEP after WAIT_END; 4 ends CHOOSER_WAIT
name       CODE:1901 CAPTION_TIME  ; CAPTION_STEP's count: a new caption at 0 (mod 20h), the empty one at 1Eh
name       CODE:1905 MENU_ENTER    ; 1 by Enter, Space, F1..F4 (MENU_KEYS)
; the chooser's end, CODE:505C to its RET (2026-09-30)
code       CODE:364F MENU_CAPTION  ; in MENU_LOOP at CODE:18FD 1: CAPTION from MENU_PICS_NOBOX while MENU_BLINK is 1, else MENU_INFO_PICS with MENU_INFO, else MENU_PICS, by MENU_ROW
code       CODE:28CF CAPTIONS_FREE ; every caption routine's block (the selectors at +4 of the 6-byte far pointers from CODE:1554 to CAPTION) freed, INT 92h AH=5
code       CODE:28F5 CHOOSER_FREE  ; CAPTIONS_FREE, then MENUCHAR_SEL, CUBE_SEL, TUBE_SEL, TORUS_SEL, TINYFONT_SEL, INFODATA_SEL and DRIVER_SEL freed (computed at CODE:521C)
code       CODE:33F5 KBD_RESTORE   ; IRQ 1 masked at the PIC, its vector back from KBD_OLD (INT 93h AH=4 BL=1) (computed at CODE:5256)
name       CODE:2B0A2 KEY_CHARS    ; 256 bytes: the keyboard table of CODE:50A9 upper-cased, FFh for no character
; the Info and greetings pages (INFO_PAGE, GREETINGS_PAGE), read 2026-09-30
code       CODE:4214 PAGE_MODE     ; video memory cleared over 8 frames (FRAME_WAIT, MUSIC_MIX each), the DAC's first 128 colours from CODE:8A3C, CRT_START 0, CRT_START_ON 0, then a 256-colour unchained mode: sequencer 0101h, 0604h, the CRTC from PAGE_CRTC (4Ch bytes a line), attribute mode 41h, GC 5 40h
name       CODE:433E PAGE_CRTC     ; PAGE_MODE's CRTC registers 0..18h
code       CODE:4357 PAGE_MODE_END ; back to the chooser's mode: the CRTC pairs at CHOOSER_CRTC, sequencer 1 09h, memory mode 06h, attribute mode 01h, GC 5 0, VIDEO_TOP_CLEAR, CRT_START_ON 1
name       CODE:43DD CHOOSER_CRTC  ; nine CRTC index, value pairs
code       CODE:2522 VIDEO_TOP_CLEAR ; video memory 0..5Bh cleared, all planes
code       CODE:43EF PAGE_BORDER   ; a frame of colour 1: the first line (4Ch bytes, all planes) and the one at 4234h, the left pixel (plane 0) and the right one (plane 3, byte 4Bh) of the lines between
code       CODE:3D72 PAGE_PAL_MAKE ; PAGE_PAL_TO from INFODATA.MGL at PAGE_BASE + 0Ah (300h bytes), colour 1 white, colour 16 (0, 0, 10h); a fade from CODE:8A3C to it (PAL_FROM, PAL_TO, CH_FADE_LEVEL 40h)
name       CODE:5A67 PAGE_PAL_TO   ; a page's palette, 300h bytes
name       CODE:5767 PAGE_PAL      ; PAGE_FADE's 128 colours (180h bytes), sent by PAGE_DAC
code       CODE:3D19 PAGE_FADE     ; while CH_FADE_LEVEL is not negative: PAGE_PAL mixed from PAL_FROM and PAL_TO as PAL_FADE does, then CH_FADE_LEVEL less CH_FADE_STEP (not held at 0)
code       CODE:3CFD PAGE_DAC      ; DAC 0..127 (180h bytes) from ESI
code       CODE:3DD7 TILE_DRAW     ; tile AL (row: high nibble, column: low) of a page's 128 x 128 picture, 8 x 8 pixels from INFODATA.MGL at PAGE_BASE + 30Ah (a line 80h bytes) to video memory 28Ah + row * 260h + column * 2
code       CODE:3FCA TILE_STEP     ; the next tile by TILE_ORDER and TILE_COUNT; TILE_ORDER FFFFFFFFh after 256
name       CODE:3B54 TILE_ORDER    ; the permutation of the tiles (CODE:4A1B), FFFFFFFFh when all are drawn
name       CODE:3B70 TILE_COUNT    ; the tiles drawn (a byte)
name       CODE:4A1B TILE_PERM     ; 256 bytes, each tile once presumably (not checked)
name       CODE:3B47 PAGE_BASE     ; the Info page's offset in INFODATA.MGL (the dword at 4 + 4 * MENU_ROW)
code       CODE:3B72 CHAR_PUT      ; tinyfont.fnt's character AL at EDI (a pixel address: plane EDI AND 3), EDI moved on by its width: a record of 4 bytes a character (+0 its bits' start, +2 the width, +3 the first line; the next record's +0 the end), a word a line of 16 pixels, pixels set to colour 1 one at a time by the map mask; the first pixel one to the right of EDI
code       CODE:3CCE CHAR_PUT_R    ; the same with EDI moved back by the width first (right-aligned text)
code       CODE:41A8 LINE_MEASURE  ; LINE_LEFT: the characters from TEXT_POS (in INFODATA.MGL) up to the last space before WRAP_WIDTH pixels, or the line's end, and the space or newline; at the text's end the characters left
code       CODE:4197 LINE_MEASURE2 ; the same with the text in CODE (GREETINGS_PAGE)
code       CODE:3FF3 TEXT_STEP     ; one character of TEXT_POS (INFODATA.MGL) drawn at TEXT_DI, LINE_LEFT counted; at 0 LINE_MEASURE and TEXT_DI to the next 48-line row's start + 4
code       CODE:405E TEXT_STEP2    ; the same with the text in CODE
name       CODE:3B4F WRAP_WIDTH    ; a line's width in pixels (A0h on the Info page, 128h on the greetings page)
name       CODE:3B64 TEXT_DI       ; the text's pixel address
name       CODE:3B71 LINE_LEFT     ; the characters left of the line
code       CODE:4442 TITLE_MAKE    ; TITLE_BUF: the five names (3 bytes) of MENU_ROW's table in HISCORES (32h bytes a table, 0Ah an entry), each ended by 0Ah, the last by 0
code       CODE:448B SCORES_MAKE   ; SCORES_BUF: the five scores from bytes +6, +7, +8, +9, +4, +5 of each entry as hex digits, low digit first, with dots after thousands; the leading zeros and dots taken off (the string is drawn right to left), 0Ah after each, 0 at the end
name       CODE:5D67 TITLE_BUF     ; TITLE_MAKE's
name       CODE:5D7B SCORES_BUF    ; SCORES_MAKE's
code       CODE:40C1 TITLE_STEP    ; a character of TITLE_TEXT at TITLE_DI (a newline: the next 48-line row + A8h), FFFFFFFFh at the end
code       CODE:412C SCORES_STEP   ; a character of SCORES_TEXT right-aligned at SCORES_DI (a newline: + 128h)
name       CODE:3B5C TITLE_TEXT    ; TITLE_BUF's next character
name       CODE:3B60 SCORES_TEXT   ; SCORES_BUF's next character
name       CODE:3B68 TITLE_DI      ; ABA8h at the start
name       CODE:3B6C SCORES_DI     ; AC28h at the start
code       CODE:2789 CUBE_DRAW_MIX ; CUBE_DRAW with MUSIC_MIX after each rotation of a plane (after the pages)
ds         CODE:9CDC-9CE3 CODE     ; DS from CODE:A10B, as KBD_IRQ
comment    CODE:9CD4 the completion routine handed with command 11h at CODE:9B31: sets CODE:9CE5 to FFh; the driver calls it from its command 6 once a jingle has ended (a jump to the order it plays, SB16.SDR +1EAF; run 2026-09-29: 1.69 s after the command 0Ah of order 0Eh)
name       CODE:B99C DRV_TICK      ; handed with command 0Eh at CODE:9B93: counts CODE:BAD4 (the blinking of display opcode 1Ah, the random awards of handler 1Ah); run 2026-09-29, table 1: 838 writes by CODE:B9AA from t=130.11 to 142, 70.5 a second, so once a frame at 70 Hz
ds         CODE:B9AA-B9B7 CODE     ; DS from CODE:A10B
comment    CODE:BAFE GAME_PHASE 0: waits for the retrace (CODE:3D372) until port 60h reads 1 (Esc pressed), then returns with the phase still 0, so CODE:B993 calls it again; nothing else, QUIT_TABLE untouched. Run 2026-09-29 (table 1, GAME_PHASE poked to 0 at t=145.156 during play, Esc at 146 and 150): 70 passes a second to t=156, AL 1 at both Esc presses and the loop went on; the screen frozen from then on. A leftover, presumably (a debug pause)
comment    CODE:BB0A after the text '9090', no reference found: a routine at CODE:BB0E in the style of CODE:BAFE (the retrace, CODE:1023E, then port 60h): keys 1/2 (scan codes 2, 3) move the word CODE:DBFE by -1/+1, keys 3/4 the word CODE:DC00 (state+10BEh..10C2h, read nowhere else; at 23Ah or more CODE:DBFC gets F001h), the screen start line CODE:A2B9 to [DC00h]-100 through CODE:9311, and the dword at DS:72h to [DC00h]*150h+[DBFEh], the form CODE:269D7 gives a ball's +72h ([CODE:0010]+72h). A debug tool that moved a point over the table and scrolled with it, presumably; dead in this release
comment    CODE:B9B9 handed with command 0Fh at CODE:9BAF (ECX from CODE:9B8E: DDDDh, E898h, EEEEh or F258h, set at CODE:9725..9882): sets CODE:BAD1 to FFh, the CRT start address from CODE:BAD2 (+54h while the word at CODE:D884 is not 0) and, when CODE:00A2 is 3, instead the attribute controller's pel panning (2, 4 or 6 as CODE:D884 is negative, 0 or positive) with the start from CODE:BAD2 alone: presumably the screen's scroll per frame, not checked
ds         CODE:B9C3-BA7A CODE     ; DS from CODE:A10B
